00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:39.750
Tax loss harvesting with exchange traded funds, or ETFs, lets you book a capital loss without

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:40.850
stepping out of the market.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:46.230
And Barron's reports the swap approach generated billions in reported tax losses last year.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:52.330
You open a taxable account at a Canadian broker, find two ETFs with overlapping holdings

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:57.510
but different tickers sell the loser to book the loss, then buy the replacement immediately.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:02.210
Think of it as selling last year's winter coat on a down day and walking into the next

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:04.990
shop for a different brand that still gets you through January.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:10.450
You never stand outside in the cold, but the old coat's loss is the receipt the tax office

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:11.010
will accept.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:16.010
The step works best when the price gap is small and the swap happens inside the same

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:20.690
trading day, because overnight drift can undo the economic equivalence you just tried

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:21.070
to keep.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:26.370
You see a U.S. listed broad market ETF in a non-registered account sitting at a loss

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:31.750
and a similar fund tracks almost the same index. Do you swap the same day or wait for

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:37.050
a wider dislocation? I'd execute the same day. Drift is the enemy of a clean harvest.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:42.530
The technique has produced consistent tax savings in years with mixed equity returns. And

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:48.270
it is particularly useful for Canadian investors holding U.S. listed ETFs in non-registered accounts

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.350
where capital gains are taxable at the inclusion rate.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:57.490
It fails when both ETFs move in lockstep or when Canada's superficial loss rules disallow

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:03.370
the claim if you or an affiliated person replace the position within 30 days, and the United

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:07.010
States wash sale rule is the parallel trap on that side of the border.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:12.450
Before you click, confirm the replacement has similar beta and sector exposure so you

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:18.170
keep the intended market position, then record the new adjusted cost base or ACB in the

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.610
account software so the next sale is not a guess.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.670
Remember, book the loss, keep the exposure.

